## Interview call reminders (release 41)

For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day''s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or **Call** for a phone call). **Today** shows **Interviews today**: each call''s time, candidate, role and its **Join** or **Call** button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role&#39;s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.</p><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-open-a-role-and-send-the-apply-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Open a role and send the apply link</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the role</b> to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); <b class="gd-ui">Close the role</b> takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role&#39;s questions, about five minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pass mark and pay</b> changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-what-happens-to-each-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens to each application</h2><p class="gd-p">The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email; their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Without a camera or a microphone they type, on the same clock. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript and the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41): at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>) with no knock-out answer, a remote applicant is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy, and a field applicant is invited to book a live call. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-field-applicants-the-live-call-before-the-townhall-release-3" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field applicants: the live call before the townhall (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant at the pass mark is hired by itself. A field applicant who passes is invited to a 10-minute live call: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone', 'chapter', 'quick-reference', 'The bell at the top of the menu opens **Alerts**: every alert for you, newest first, with the number not yet read. The same alerts reach your phone when phone alerts are on. Nothing to set up.

## The list

1. Press the bell. **All**, **Unread** or **Urgent** narrows the list.
2. Press an alert to open its page; it is marked read. **Mark read** or **Mark all read** clears without opening.
3. **Snooze 30 min** on an urgent alert: it comes again in 30 minutes and is not passed on meanwhile.

Red dot: urgent and unread. Black dot: unread.

## What alerts you

| Group | Alerts |
| --- | --- |
| Leads | New renter lead (form, phone number box, game claim, live chat), request typed and not sent, new owner lead and unfinished application, visitor turning Hot |
| Bookings | Confirmed, going out, back, closed, no-show (urgent), cancelled, offer sent, viewed, accepted and about to expire, extension asked or paid, change asked or applied, deposit released, insurer booking with no claim number |
| Money | Payment of $500 or more, refund, deposit hold failed and card declined at pickup (urgent), owner debit failed (urgent), investor money, the 9 pm cash summary |
| Field work | Job assigned, started, finished, running late (urgent), checklist incomplete, fuel or km off at return |
| Documents | Licence to review, agreement signed, agreement not signed 2 hours before pickup (urgent), insurance proof missing 24 hours before |
| Customers | Reviews (3 stars or less urgent), complaint words in chat, texts or emails, account deletion asked (urgent), unsubscribes and STOP (in Alerts only) |
| Fleet | Tracker offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery (urgent), service due (in Alerts only), car paused or unpublished |
| Owners and investors | Owner gives notice (urgent), owner banking changed (urgent), investor signed |
| System | Admin sign-in from a new device or country (urgent), many failed sign-ins (urgent), deploy finished or failed, usage over 80% and data health (in Alerts only) |
| Staff and hiring | Academy lessons, quizzes failed twice, certified; Sales late or idle in their hours; new application, AI interview scored, link expired, offer accepted |
| Wins | First booking of a car, record day or week, an owner''s first payout, the month''s totals on the 1st |
| Briefs | 8 am morning brief, 9 pm evening wrap; an urgent alert nobody opened |

Also a line for each important message sent to a renter, owner or investor (late notices and the return-time notice are urgent).

## Buttons on a phone alert

- **Call**: opens your phone''s dialer with the lead''s or renter''s number (the Quo app if it handles your calls).
- **Send offer**, **Approve** or **Decline**, **Mark picked up**: open the booking where you do it. Nothing is decided from the lock screen.
- **Snooze 30 min** on urgent alerts.

## Who gets what

- Customer service, Sales and Fleet get their function''s alerts while on duty (Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes), and what is assigned to them. Field staff get their jobs. Each gets a morning brief of their own work at 8 am.
- An urgent alert a team member did not open in 15 minutes goes to the next person on duty, then to you after another 15.
- More than 5 alerts of one kind in 10 minutes reach the phone once, as a group; each stays in the list.
- Test and verification accounts never get alerts, and a test address never makes one.

## Settings

**Alerts** > **Settings**:

1. **Phone alerts**: turn them on for this device, choose the topics, or keep a different choice on this device only.
2. **Quiet hours** (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them): normal alerts wait until they end. Urgent alerts always come.
3. **Focus mode** for 1 or 3 hours: only urgent alerts reach your phone; the rest wait in the list.
4. **Which alerts staff get**: each kind on or off, and urgent, normal or digest.

> Tip: the full table of every alert and every role is docs/alerts/matrix.md in the code.

## Alerts by email

Staff and Admin alerts that are not urgent no longer come one email each: they come together in one email at most once an hour, with everything since the last one. Urgent ones still come on their own, at most 3 an hour: a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, and the site down. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once either way. Choose under **Settings** > **My profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.

## One alert per booking moment (release 35)
- A car not back gets one alert per booking and return time, for example "CC-10077 not back: due 5:00 pm, renter reminded, return check-in not started", with **Call** and **Open**. It goes to the Admins, the person on the return job and Fleet, each once.
- What we send the renter about a booking is in the booking''s activity, not an alert of its own.
- The renter''s overdue reminders wait 15 minutes after the return time (Program settings, late chase grace) and stop once staff press **Returning now**, the return job starts, or the tracker shows the car at our location.
- Alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, grouped by kind, newest first; each stays in the list with its own link.
', 'Alerts: the bell and your phone', 'Every alert for you in one list, the buttons on a phone alert, quiet hours, focus mode, and which alerts staff get.',
  'The bell at the top of the menu opens **Alerts**: every alert for you, newest first, with the number not yet read. The same alerts reach your phone when phone alerts are on. Nothing to set up.

## The list

1. Press the bell. **All**, **Unread** or **Urgent** narrows the list.
2. Press an alert to open its page; it is marked read. **Mark read** or **Mark all read** clears without opening.
3. **Snooze 30 min** on an urgent alert: it comes again in 30 minutes and is not passed on meanwhile.

Red dot: urgent and unread. Black dot: unread.

## What alerts you

| Group | Alerts |
| --- | --- |
| Leads | New renter lead (form, phone number box, game claim, live chat), request typed and not sent, new owner lead and unfinished application, visitor turning Hot |
| Bookings | Confirmed, going out, back, closed, no-show (urgent), cancelled, offer sent, viewed, accepted and about to expire, extension asked or paid, change asked or applied, deposit released, insurer booking with no claim number |
| Money | Payment of $500 or more, refund, deposit hold failed and card declined at pickup (urgent), owner debit failed (urgent), investor money, the 9 pm cash summary |
| Field work | Job assigned, started, finished, running late (urgent), checklist incomplete, fuel or km off at return |
| Documents | Licence to review, agreement signed, agreement not signed 2 hours before pickup (urgent), insurance proof missing 24 hours before |
| Customers | Reviews (3 stars or less urgent), complaint words in chat, texts or emails, account deletion asked (urgent), unsubscribes and STOP (in Alerts only) |
| Fleet | Tracker offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery (urgent), service due (in Alerts only), car paused or unpublished |
| Owners and investors | Owner gives notice (urgent), owner banking changed (urgent), investor signed |
| System | Admin sign-in from a new device or country (urgent), many failed sign-ins (urgent), deploy finished or failed, usage over 80% and data health (in Alerts only) |
| Staff and hiring | Academy lessons, quizzes failed twice, certified; Sales late or idle in their hours; new applicant and AI interview done with its outcome (for your information), live call booked (also a To-do), interview call reminders (the morning of, an hour before the first call, 10 minutes before each), link expired, offer accepted; townhall reminders (the day before, the morning of, an hour and 15 minutes before) |
| Wins | First booking of a car, record day or week, an owner''s first payout, the month''s totals on the 1st |
| Briefs | 8 am morning brief, 9 pm evening wrap; an urgent alert nobody opened |

Also a line for each important message sent to a renter, owner or investor (late notices and the return-time notice are urgent).

## Buttons on a phone alert

- **Call**: opens your phone''s dialer with the lead''s or renter''s number (the Quo app if it handles your calls).
- **Send offer**, **Approve** or **Decline**, **Mark picked up**: open the booking where you do it. Nothing is decided from the lock screen.
- **Snooze 30 min** on urgent alerts.

## Who gets what

- Customer service, Sales and Fleet get their function''s alerts while on duty (Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes), and what is assigned to them. Field staff get their jobs. Each gets a morning brief of their own work at 8 am.
- An urgent alert a team member did not open in 15 minutes goes to the next person on duty, then to you after another 15.
- More than 5 alerts of one kind in 10 minutes reach the phone once, as a group; each stays in the list.
- Test and verification accounts never get alerts, and a test address never makes one.

## Settings

**Alerts** > **Settings**:

1. **Phone alerts**: turn them on for this device, choose the topics, or keep a different choice on this device only.
2. **Quiet hours** (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them): normal alerts wait until they end. Urgent alerts always come.
3. **Focus mode** for 1 or 3 hours: only urgent alerts reach your phone; the rest wait in the list.
4. **Which alerts staff get**: each kind on or off, and urgent, normal or digest.

> Tip: the full table of every alert and every role is docs/alerts/matrix.md in the code.

## Alerts by email

Staff and Admin alerts that are not urgent no longer come one email each: they come together in one email at most once an hour, with everything since the last one. Urgent ones still come on their own, at most 3 an hour: a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, and the site down. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once either way. Choose under **Settings** > **My profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.

## One alert per booking moment (release 35)
- A car not back gets one alert per booking and return time, for example "CC-10077 not back: due 5:00 pm, renter reminded, return check-in not started", with **Call** and **Open**. It goes to the Admins, the person on the return job and Fleet, each once.
- What we send the renter about a booking is in the booking''s activity, not an alert of its own.
- The renter''s overdue reminders wait 15 minutes after the return time (Program settings, late chase grace) and stop once staff press **Returning now**, the return job starts, or the tracker shows the car at our location.
- Alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, grouped by kind, newest first; each stays in the list with its own link.
