3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")

## Clock in and out

Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press **Clock in** on your home page when you start and **Clock out** when you stop. **My hours** shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.

## Breaks and activity (release 35)

Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press **Start break** next to the clock (a reason is optional) and **End break** when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on **My hours**; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.

While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks **Still there?**: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the **Call** button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: the academy first, then your staff agreement (it opens for signing once the academy is passed), then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: the academy, your staff agreement, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.</p><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-menu" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The menu</h2><p class="gd-p">Every office role has the same short menu: <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one <b class="gd-ui">More</b> for the rest of your work, <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> on Requests, <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters&#39; phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.</p><p class="gd-p">A <b class="gd-ui">More</b> page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Function</th><th scope="col">Your links, then More</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button)</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">To do</h2><p class="gd-p">Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows your function, today&#39;s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Next up</b> is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service and Sales: <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for a reply</b> lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today&#39;s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every open task</b>: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Sheet</b> opens the step-by-step procedure.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day&#39;s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">On a computer, press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:20.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.9%;top:52.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:72.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-work-a-task" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a task</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open the working screen</b></td><td>Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Done</b></td><td>You finished it. It leaves the queue.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b></td><td>You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Escalate</b></td><td>It needs an Admin. Add why.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Hand over</b></td><td>Give it to someone else on the team.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b></td><td>Leave a note for whoever looks next.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-today" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Today</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press a booking number to open it. <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> takes you back to your tasks.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/today</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/700"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="700"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:24.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-documents-to-sign" data-g